  "foaf:name": "Pacific solutions to save our ocean: an integrated ocean science programme towards a healthy Blue Pacific Continent to sustain future generations.",
  "sdo:name": "Pacific solutions to save our ocean: an integrated ocean science programme towards a healthy Blue Pacific Continent to sustain future generations.",
  "sdo:description": "This Ocean Decade action aims to leverage the spate of national ocean policies launched (NOPs) in the Pacific in recent years that all address a need for greater integrated ocean management (IOM). This action seeks to increase scientific capacity and create opportunities for ocean science to feed into decision making. This will be achieved by focusing on three major aspects including regulatory frameworks, decision support systems, and increased considerations for Pacific culture and context. As custodians of the world&#x27;s largest marine ecosystems, the Blue Pacific Continent, we seek to save our Ocean and provide solutions to some of our existential challenges such as climate change.",
  "sdo:location": "New Caledonia",
  "sdo:identifier": "84",
  "sdo:url": "https://oceandecade.org/actions/pacific-solutions-to-save-our-ocean/",
  "sdo:license": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/",
  "sdo:parentOrganization": {
    "@type": "sdo:Organization",
    "sdo:name": "Pacific Community (SPC)"
  },
  "sdo:keywords": [
    {
      "@type": "sdo:DefinedTerm",
      "sdo:name": "Decade Programme",
      "sdo:description": "A Programme is typically global or regional in scale and contributes to the achievement of one or more of the Decade Challenges. It is long-term (multi-year), interdisciplinary, and consists of component Decade Projects and potentially enabling Decade Activities.",
